    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Concept Overview</h2>
        <ul style="list-style-type: disc; margin-left: 1.5rem;">
            <li><strong>Input Functions</strong>: Using `input()` to pause execution and get user data.</li>
            <li><strong>Exception Handling</strong>: Using `try/except ValueError` to prevent crashes when users type text instead of numbers.</li>
            <li><strong>Logic Loops</strong>: `while True:` keeps asking until valid input is received.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Common Misconceptions</h2>
        <div class="info-content">
            <p><strong>1. Zero-Based Indexing</strong></p>
            <p>The user sees options 1, 2, 3. The list indices are 0, 1, 2. The code must subtract 1 (`choice = int(...) - 1`).</p>
            
            <p><strong>2. Infinite Loops</strong></p>
            <p>Students often forget to `return` or `break` inside the valid check, causing the game to ask forever even if correct.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section">
        <h2 class="oop-section-title">Solution Code</h2>
        <div class="code-block" style="background: #1e1e1e; color: #d4d4d4; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto;">
            <pre><code>    def respond_to_npc(self, options):
        # We need to pick an index from the options list
        while True:
            try:
                # 1. Get input
                raw = input("Choose an option: ")
                
                # 2. Convert to int and shift to 0-based
                choice = int(raw) - 1
                
                # 3. Validate logical range
                if 0 <= choice < len(options):
                    return choice  # Success! Exit loop/method
                
                print("Invalid choice. Try again.")
                
            except ValueError:
                # User typed "hello" instead of "1"
                print("Please enter a number.")</code></pre>
        </div>
    </section>

